(Ravik Rail Link adds two freight paths for the summer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Ravik Rail Link will run additional freight paths each weekday from) Tj
T*
(June to August.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Paths leave early in the morning and in the late afternoon. All take grain) Tj
T*
(wagons and general freight.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The link says the extra paths are for scheduled traffic and are not a) Tj
T*
(reserve for spot cargoes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Road hauliers will keep their existing access to the terminal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The extra paths are aimed at seasonal demand from grain and general freight) Tj
T*
(customers, and the link says they will be reviewed at the end of the summer. The) Tj
T*
(timetable has been adjusted so that the new paths do not delay the existing) Tj
T*
(passenger service. Freight customers have been told that wagon availability,) Tj
T*
(rather than track capacity, is the main constraint on bookings. The link's) Tj
T*
(office will publish any changes to the schedule in the usual way.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The link says the extra paths are a trial and will be kept only if demand) Tj
T*
(holds. It has asked freight customers to book in advance. The timetable change) Tj
T*
(does not affect passenger services. The office will publish a revised notice if) Tj
T*
(the trial is extended.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] A revised timetable is available from the link's office.) Tj
T*
() Tj
